\section*{Abstract}
Traditional geophysical management relies on passive hazard monitoring and reactive disaster response. This monograph presents a closed-loop planetary control architecture---the Global Hyper-Conductive Geothermal Grid (G2G)---that actively regulates tectonic stress and planetary radiative balance. By unifying rate-and-state friction mechanics with top-of-atmosphere radiative transfer through a decentralized AI fusion core, we formulate a two-layer feedback controller with Lyapunov-stable envelopes. Numerical simulations confirm that the coupled system rejects severe tectonic disturbances without dynamic rupture or climate overshoot.

