\section{Introduction}
Planetary engineering requires transitioning from descriptive geodynamics to normative, closed-loop control. Active fault zones accumulate shear stress $\sigma$ governed by pore-fluid pressure $p_f$ and frictional state $\theta$, while geothermal extraction influences surface temperature $T_s$ and radiative flux $R$. This monograph introduces an integrated architecture coupling deep-Earth stabilization with radiative homeostasis.

