\section{Numerical Validation}

A stiff Radau solver integrates the coupled system over 30 days. A tectonic disturbance is introduced:
\begin{equation}
V_{\text{plate}}(t) =
\begin{cases}
V_0, & t < 15\ \text{days},\\
3V_0, & t \ge 15\ \text{days}.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

Results show:
\begin{itemize}
\item Slip velocity $V$ remains in the aseismic envelope.
\item Pore pressure $p_f$ adjusts smoothly.
\item Radiative flux $R$ remains near zero.
\item Surface temperature $T_s$ stays bounded.
\end{itemize}

